WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.140
Which Dutch law applies to us,
and who in this room owns the answer?

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.480
Two laws started on the same day,
15 August 2026.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.360
First, which law applies.

00:00:11.715 --> 00:00:13.985
The Cbw covers your systems.

00:00:14.355 --> 00:00:18.865
It applies to about 8,000 organisations,
and you assess yourself.

00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:23.115
The Wwke covers buildings,
people and recovery.

00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:28.805
It applies to about 500, and only after
your sector minister designates you.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.850
A critical entity under the Wwke is
an essential entity under the Cbw.

00:00:35.255 --> 00:00:36.745
The reverse does not hold.

00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:41.607
Second, the Wwke adds the
building and the people.

00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:44.487
It asks about floods, fire, sabotage

00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:46.967
and a supplier that stops delivering.

00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:48.197
After designation,

00:00:48.907 --> 00:00:53.337
it requires a risk assessment within
nine months, and measures within ten.

00:00:53.657 --> 00:00:57.147
Those measures include background
checks for critical roles.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.387
Third, two clocks.

00:00:59.772 --> 00:01:01.742
Under the Wwke,

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:07.022
a significant disruption goes to the
competent authority within 24 hours.

00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:08.682
Under the Cbw,

00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:11.902
it is an early warning within 24 hours,

00:01:12.352 --> 00:01:17.282
a notification within 72 hours,
and a final report within one month.

00:01:17.562 --> 00:01:21.632
A fire that takes down a data hall
can start both clocks at once.

00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:24.867
Fourth, the gap between two programmes.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:29.577
Facilities, HR and IT can each
assess half of the same site.

00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:34.457
Two parallel programmes cost more, and
leave the gap between them with no owner.

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:36.967
We suggest one board decision instead.

00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:39.293
What good looks like.

00:01:39.578 --> 00:01:41.308
One executive owns resilience,

00:01:41.738 --> 00:01:43.008
cyber and physical.

00:01:43.378 --> 00:01:45.968
One risk assessment per essential service.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:49.168
One incident process,
with two report templates.

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:51.898
One evidence file for both supervisors.

00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:54.563
The Cbw names the management body,

00:01:54.563 --> 00:01:58.573
and requires it to approve the
measures and follow training.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:01.640
A suggested first step.

00:02:01.925 --> 00:02:06.395
Ask legal to settle scope now,
not after a designation letter arrives.

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:10.135
Then date and sign one
decision that covers both laws.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.520
The law does not care whether a
hacker or a flood stopped the service.

00:02:15.845 --> 00:02:17.775
Decide once, and name the owner.

